    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field on the owner resource so it returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 **and** an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing project conventions (the DTOs are generated from the OpenAPI spec at build time, and computed read-only fields are populated in the MapStruct mapper):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `membershipNumber`), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a `membershipTier(Owner)` default method mirroring the style of the existing `membershipNumber`/`displayName`/`initials` helpers. It returns `SILVER` only when `namesakeCount == 0` and a non-blank email is present, and `BRONZE` otherwise (null-safe).\n\nTest results:\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (unique owner + email \u2192 SILVER) \u2705\n- `AcceptanceTest.functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (no email \u2192 BRONZE) \u2705\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**",
